as from Louisiana, which does not hold traditional primary elections. 

These data were collected by Michael G. Miller (mgmiller@barnard.edu) and Nicki Camberg, both of Barnard College. If you publish with these data, please cite as:

Miller, Michael G., and Nicki Camberg. 2020. “U.S. House Primary Election Results (2012-2018).” Harvard Dataverse, Version 1. 

This file employs the same architecture as the following dataset:

Pettigrew, Stephen; Owen, Karen; Wanless, Emily, 2014, "U.S. House Primary Election Results (1956-2010)," available at https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/26448. Current version information can be found at the preceding link. 

